# Ticket git workflow

This repo **does** want commits without the user asking again. Implementing a ticket is the request.

Default branch is **`master`**. Do not push unless the user asks. Do not `--force` on `master`. Do not skip hooks. Do not amend commits you did not just create on this branch.

## One branch per ticket

Before editing application code for a ticket (e.g. `T02-04`):

1. `git status` / `git diff` — do not mix another ticket’s files onto this branch.
2. If you are not already on the ticket branch, start it from **current `master`**:

```text
git checkout master
git checkout -b ticket/T02-04-full-and-limited-datablocks
```

Branch name: `ticket/<ticket-id>-<short-slug>` from the ticket filename (`T02-04-full-and-limited-datablocks`).

Never commit ticket work directly on `master`. Never reuse one branch for two ticket IDs.

## Progressive commits

Follow `.cursor/rules/progressive-commits.mdc` for **all** application work (tickets, bugfixes, requested changes). Commit each slice as you go; do not wait for a second ask. Include the ticket id in the message when there is one.

## Merge into master when the ticket is done

Only when that ticket’s ACs are satisfied (or the user says the ticket is done):

```text
git checkout master
git merge --no-ff ticket/T02-04-full-and-limited-datablocks -m "$(cat <<'EOF'
Merge ticket/T02-04-full-and-limited-datablocks

Full/limited datablocks with Mode C hundreds (T02-04).
EOF
)"
```

`--no-ff` so each ticket stays a merge on `master`. After a clean merge, delete the **local** ticket branch. Do not start the next ticket until `master` has this merge.

If merge conflicts: stop, report them, do not force. If the user is mid-review on the ticket branch, do not merge until they say so.

## Whole-phase agents

Still **one branch per ticket**. Finish → merge to `master` → next ticket from updated `master`.

## Swarm override (`phases/SWARM.md`)

If the session is a **swarm orchestrator or phase captain**: ticket workers **do not merge**. The captain holds the merge lock (`--no-ff` onto `master`, then `npm test`). Workers only return `READY TO MERGE`. Max 3 workers in flight.
